<title>USA: Universal Health sees 1996 EPS up 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Universal Health sees 1996 EPS up 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KING OF PRUSSIA, Penn. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Universal Health Services Inc said on Thursday that it expects an increase in earnings per share of 30 percent and net income of 40 percent for the full year 1996 compared to 1995.</p>
<p>The company said that net revenues for the 1996 year exceeded $1.1 billion with net income of $50 million. The company's debt at year end 1996 was $285 million.</p>
<p>Universal Health, a hospital management company, will announce fourth quarter and full year results on February 13, 1997.</p>
<p>	  -- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
